{
  "id": "axonal-myelination",
  "term": "axonal myelination",
  "definition": "Axonal myelination is the formation or restoration of myelin around axons in the central nervous system. This myelin is needed for neurons to function properly, and when it is lost or not regenerated, neurons are more vulnerable to further degeneration.",
